      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TALISKER SKIPPER (5) again drew a wide gate last start but did a good job, beaten 4 metres into second at Kilmore over 2180m. Taking on a better field but he is up to the task. CATIES SON (8) finished ninth last start over 1690m at Kilmore, beaten 15 metres, after a good third there the run prior. Will enjoy a pretty soft run from this draw, with the sprint lane to play a big role. Certainly cannot be faulted after that last effort and is good enough to win a race of this calibre. MONSIEUR FLAMEL (6) was responsible for a better effort last time out when runner-up over 1720m at Melton. Should run a big race. CRESCO THREEPEAT (7) must be respected after scoring last start by 1.4 metres at Albury over 1770m. Hard to knock winning form.",
